=== p2-windows · W7 · page:onboarding/Onboarding (WinUI 3 / Fluent) ===
Parity unit : page:onboarding/Onboarding   kind=page   web route=/onboarding
Web source  : web/src/features/onboarding/pages/OnboardingPage.tsx
ADR refs    : ADR-002, ADR-004, ADR-005, ADR-006, ADR-011, ADR-013, ADR-014, ADR-015
Runner      : .NET 10.0.300 SDK present (dotnet --version 10.0.300) — NOT blocked.

=== APPROACH ===
- The repository's WinUI app is code-first C# (no .xaml page files); every feature surface lives under
  apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/feature-views/<Name>/ as <Name>.Model.cs (pure, Microsoft.UI-free projection,
  unit-tested headlessly), <Name>.Source.cs (the generated-client feed), <Name>.ViewModel.cs
  (INotifyPropertyChanged + IDisposable state holder) and <Name>.cs (the Fluent view), exactly as the sibling W7
  ExportsPage / DashboardPage do. The generated prompt's idealized "OnboardingPage.xaml + OnboardingPageViewModel.cs
  under TeslaSync/Features/Onboarding" is mapped onto these real conventions (namespace TeslaSync.App.FeatureViews.Onboarding).
- Navigation entry (ADR / W4 seam): the route "Onboarding" (RouteTable.cs path `onboarding`, public/auth:false) was a
  W4 dual-purpose surface — the Windows shell uses it both as the web /onboarding destination AND as the signed-out
  auth gate (ShellWindow.NavigateTo redirects protected routes to "onboarding" when signed out). The web /onboarding
  is purely the first-run setup checklist (shown post-auth via OnboardingGate); the only interactive sign-in entry on
  Windows is the W4 OnboardingView. To deliver web parity WITHOUT bypassing the predecessor sign-in, the registration
  (ShellWindow.xaml.cs) is now an auth-aware factory: AppAuth.IsAuthenticated -> the W7 FeatureViews.Onboarding.OnboardingPage
  checklist; otherwise -> the W4 OnboardingView sign-in. The checklist's internal CTAs (Connect Tesla account, footer
  account link, Skip, Continue) raise NavigationRequested -> ShellWindow.NavigateTo (routes /tesla-account, /); its
  documentation links raise DocumentationRequested -> ShellWindow.OpenDocumentation (Launcher against the API origin).
- Data binding (ADR-004): the manifest data source is useOnboardingStatus (GET /onboarding/status). The view-model reads
  through an injected IOnboardingStatusFeed; the default EmptyOnboardingStatusFeed resolves the pessimistic "nothing
  connected" snapshot (the outstanding checklist — the host-injection precedent the sibling W7 pages set), and the
  generated-client-backed OnboardingStatusClientFeed (OnboardingPage.Source.cs) binds to the generated OpenAPI contract
  client operation get_api_v1_onboarding_status (no params, present in Generated/Api/ApiEndpoints.cs). No HTTP touches
  the view. The status JSON round-trips through the tolerant OnboardingStatusSnapshot.FromJson (snake_case fields
  tesla_connected / vehicle_count / data_flowing / is_complete; accepts the platform {data:…} envelope + missing fields).
- Two data states (manifest: loading -> success): the web page gates only the PageContainer spinner on isLoading and
  then renders the checklist for every resolved value; its useOnboardingStatus is pessimistic (retry:2, and an
  undefined result reads as "nothing connected"), so a failed read DEGRADES to the checklist with every step
  outstanding rather than a dedicated failure region. The native port reproduces exactly these two states per ADR-006:
  loading -> TsSkeleton shimmer inside GlassPanel1; success -> the intro header + 3-step Stepper + footer. The
  GlassPanel is always visible (body switches loading<->content) so the region never collapses. A feed exception is
  caught in OnboardingPageViewModel.LoadAsync and degraded to OnboardingStatusSnapshot.Pending (web pessimistic gate),
  asserted by ViewModel_feed_failure_degrades_to_the_pessimistic_checklist.
- Live freshness / polling (ADR-013): the web refetchInterval (30s until is_complete) is reproduced by a
  DispatcherQueueTimer (OnboardingRegistration.PollIntervalSeconds=30) started on Loaded and stopped on is_complete /
  Unload; OnboardingPageViewModel.ShouldPoll (resolved && !is_complete) is the contract, asserted by
  ViewModel_polls_until_complete. This surface has no SSE/live signal source and no >2-min staleness pill (status is a
  REST read, not a telemetry stream).
- Stepper parity: OnboardingProjection derives each step's done flag (tesla_connected / vehicle_count>0 / data_flowing),
  the "current" step (first not-done, web Stepper.stateOf) and the per-step CTA (tesla -> Navigate /tesla-account;
  vehicle -> Refresh, label "Checking…"/"Refresh" by isFetching; telemetry -> DocumentationLink /docs/fleet-telemetry-setup),
  rendered by OnboardingPage.cs#BuildStepRow (done=check glyph, current=ProgressRing, pending=number + connector line).
- SI units N/A (no unit-bearing fields — three booleans + a vehicle count only); no charts, no maps on this surface.
- i18n (ADR-014): all 25 onboarding.* keys are present verbatim (web key names) in Strings/en/Resources.resw as
  translation.onboarding.* with the web English values; the surface resolves them through the ILocalizer facade with the
  web key names + English defaults (PassthroughLocalizer in tests records every key). The ar/he catalogs lag en by
  design (translations land later); the app falls back to the English default via ILocalizer until translated.
- a11y (ADR-015): GlassPanel1 + each step row carry AutomationProperties.Name; the skip affordance carries its hint as
  ToolTip + AutomationProperties.HelpText; decorative indicators/chips are AccessibilityView.Raw; the page exposes a
  Group automation peer; tokens drive light/dark.

